 "title": "The Art of Giving People Exactly What They Want",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator discusses an underrated social etiquette regarding gift-giving. Instead of guessing and risking getting something they dislike, you should simply ask people what they want.",
 "key_points": [
  "If you don't know what to gift someone, ask them.",
  "Most of the time when people guess gifts, recipients do not like them but won't show it.",
  "When you ask people what they want for their birthday or anything, they will precisely tell you.",
  "People's answers are often completely different from what you would have thought they wanted.",
  "It is completely okay to ask, and there is nothing embarrassing about it."
 ],
 "content": "Social skills :- The Art of Giving People Exactly What They Want. If you don't know what to gift someone, then ask them. Now, this is one of the most underrated social etiquettes and social skills. Because most of the times when you don't know what to gift someone, you just give them anything. And they may or may not like it. Most of the times they don't like it, but they won't show it to you. So, one of the best things you can do is just ask them. Because when you ask them what they want for their birthday or anything, then they will precisely tell you what they want. Because most of the times, I have done the same thing. And the answers that people give me of what they want as a gift is like completely different from what I thought they wanted. So, it's okay. You can ask them, there's nothing embarrassing about it. \n\nScreen text: Social skills :- The Art of Giving People Exactly What They Want. If you don't know what to gift someone, then ask them. Now, this is one of the most underrated social etiquettes and social skills. Because most of the times when you don't know what to gift someone, you just give them anything. And they may or may not like it. Most of the times they don't like it, but they won't show it to you. So, one of the best things you can do is just ask them. Because when you ask them what they want for their birthday or anything, then they will precisely tell you what they want. Because most of the times, I have done the same thing. And the answers that people give me of what they want as a gift is like completely different from what I thought they wanted. So, it's okay. You can ask them, there's nothing embarrassing about it.",
